FiZWwyNzkwOTc5NjY=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:core","name":"topic:core","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":1327318271,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMzI3MzE4Mjcx","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/crash","name":"crash","color":"885544","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":11,"created_at":"2025-02-26T18:19:54Z","updated_at":"2025-02-27T17:13:37Z","closed_at":"2025-02-27T17:13:27Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103329","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103329","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103329.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103329.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Issue: The `Array::get(int p_idx)` function in Godot calls `operator[](p_idx)`, which does not perform bounds checking, leading to a crash when accessing an out-of-bounds index.\r\n\r\nSolution: Add `ERR_FAIL_INDEX_MSG(p_idx, size(), Variant());` in `get()` and `operator[]` to prevent invalid memory access and ensure safe error handling.\r\n\r\nFixes #103328\r\n\r\n\r\nPR adds bounds checking to both `Array::get(int p_idx)` and `Array::operator[](int p_idx)` so that invalid accesses are caught and handled with a proper error message. `operator[]` could probably be reverted to its previous state for performance reasons if necessary.\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/follo